The native adaptation proves actual-coordinate evaluation-kernel
inclusions, actual line evaluations, and the source point-ideal generator
changes used in the secant and tangent constructions. The required units
are constructed from the nonzero root difference in the distinct-x case,
and from a nonzero Jacobian partial in the tangent case. The common-ideal
unit then gives the actual scaled pair-product identity, conditional on the
scalar line-norm equation.

That scalar cubic line-factor equation, derived from the two source curve
equations and the secant or tangent slope, remains open. Consequently this
conditional scaled identity is not a proof of Mathlib's
XYIdeal_mul_XYIdeal theorem: its full ideal-product conclusion has not been
completed. Fractional ideals, class groups, and the full FLT proof are also
outside this attribution's scope. Native proof authoring carries no proof
authority; all saved terms are checked by Lim.
